    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0806" n="694" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg694"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Lyon to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-04-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 16, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 232.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    Liberian commission referred to in my No. 222, diplomatic, and dated January 25,
                    1908, consisting of Ex-president Dr. G. W. Gibson, Vice President J. J. Dossen,
                    and Attorney C. B. Dunbar, together with C. R. Branch and T. J. R. Faulkner as
                    attachés, will leave here the 17th instant, via Hamburg, Germany, for the United
                    States of America.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ernest Lyon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
